{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1509671-v20-feeding-ghouls-monthly-a-must","id":1509671,"title":"V20 - Feeding Ghouls monthly a must?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-25T18:29:40-07:00","id":1509671,"title":"V20 - Feeding Ghouls monthly a must?","content":"I'm asking this as a V20 question, cos blood points are involved. <br /> <br /> Reading up on ghouls and revenats, and it states under aging that ghouls are required to be fed vitae monthly or they will start aging (or die for older ghouls). <br /> <br /> But at the same time, ghouls can carry more then 1 BP in their blood pool. With older ghouls able to carry more. <br /> <br /> So if a ghoul has 2 BP or more, does this means they can surive for up to a few months (1 extra month for each BP) without being fed more vitae from their domitor? <br /> <br /> Or is the feeding of vitae each month a must regardless of their BP. <br /> <br /> *I know most vampire would not waste unnecessary vitae on a ghoul, but I'm wondering what happens, if a vampire requires their ghoul to be away from their side for a prolonged period.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26067-wingstorm","name":"Wingstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T18:36:56-07:00","id":1509672,"title":"","content":"I say a ghoul needs to burn 1 BP per month to stay a ghoul, so yes if you were playing with me and had a ghoul with 3 Blood Points you could stay a ghoul for 3 months without feeding, provided you didn't spend the blood on anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T05:21:04-07:00","id":1509706,"title":"","content":"I think this always was the case no? You need a drink 1/month to remain a ghoul irrespective of your current blood. It's why you're still a ghoul if you burn all the blood before the month is over - you got your infusion directly from a cainite.<br /> <br /> Which gives a slight benefit to tremere who can just give their ghouls some vials of preserved blood to drink every month coupled with Dominate 2 <b>ONLY DRINK ONE PER MONTH</b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12911-lateral-psychotropy","name":"Lateral.Psychotropy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-16T07:10:36-07:00","id":1511797,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the late follow up. <br /> <br /> \u200bThe question is since BPs are &quot;used up&quot; 1 each month (assuming no use of disciplines), would carrying more BPs in their system allow a ghoul to sustain their existence beyond the 1 month. Or is the act of drinking blood each month actually what makes a ghoul a ghoul. <br /> <br /> This leads to a bunch of questions, like how would ghouls work for vampires in the past? Like the dark ages, where travel is slow and a ghoul might need to be away from their master for months. For trade, missions, etc. (assuming non-Tremere, without any special blood preservation method etc). Do they have the flexibility to move around, abit still on a leash? Or are they so tied up to a dominator, that the vampire has to literally keep any useful ghouls on a short distance from them, in order to keep them fed monthly?<br /> <br /> And most importantly for role play. Even if a ghoul could last on their BP &quot;reserves&quot; for months, would their addiction to vampire vitae have consequences if they can't get their &quot;fix&quot; monthly? Would such a ghoul, far from their master, start to lose control? Start craving blood? Go into rage? Etc?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26067-wingstorm","name":"Wingstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-16T13:41:15-07:00","id":1511819,"title":"","content":"I think different editions treat how many BP a ghoul can have at any one time differently. I think V20 limits this to only 2 BP, but this can increase a little if the ghoul survives for centuries. Other editions may handle this differently or neglect to provide any details at all.<br /> <br /> But assuming the ghoul still has vitae in their system, then they remain a ghoul even if they don't get fresh vitae for that month. Once the vitae BP reaches zero, then they are no longer a ghoul - they lose any powers and age catches up to them. That is how I've always seen it play out.<br /> <br /> In terms of a ghoul being away from their domitor for an extended period of time, I think there are several ways to handle it. I think most STs would allow vitae to be stored in a container, and the ghoul could consume such &quot;cold&quot; vitae and still count. Or the domitor makes sure to send a relatively young ghoul so the aging issue doesn't come up. The ghoul stops being a ghoul and loses any powers, but is still blood bonded and presumably would still carry out its mission. Or the vampire just doesn't send out a ghoul - preferring mortal pawns or a retainer who is simply blood-bonded, but not an actual ghoul.<br /> <br /> In terms of craving fresh vitae and being addicted, I think that's really a question of ST preference combined with the specifics of the character. It's more about roleplaying than mechanics. Attributes like Nature, Willpower, and Self-Control could matter, but I'd probably use more of the character's history, relationships, and personality as to how I'd roleplay out the NPC's reaction. For some, it may just be a craving that eventually goes away with time. For others, they'd become desperate for a hit and would be willing to do anything to get it. Lots of things can be justified. Different people react to addictions and withdrawal in different ways, and I think it'd be the same for former ghouls. Do what makes sense for the character and story being done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T07:44:52-07:00","id":1511869,"title":"","content":"Ok so I'll clarify my position a little better if it was confusing.<br /> <br /> If a ghoul has 3 BPs he can stay a ghoul for 3 months as long as he uses all three BPs 1 per month to stay a ghoul. It's the ghoul using the vitae to maintain ghoul status, just like he could have burned a BP to heal a wound or pump up his strength by one in a fight.<br /> <br /> I know some people want to say the vampire has to feed them with the specific ritual purpose of the blood point keeping him a ghoul each and every month. This isn't true by the rules nor fiction its just some home brew. It is the ghoul burning one of it's BPs to stay a ghoul, period. Look to Prias for the earliest example of how this works. He would hunt and drain vampires then kill them so that he never drank from the same vampire more than once to avoid being blood bound again. His staked victim wasn't doing him a solid keeping him alive just before he cut their head off, nor was he taking out a vampire every month for years on end. Think how devastating that would have been to the Chicago vampire population. The independent ghoul hunter who is in it for the blood of his vampire victims is actually an arch type in the game. So is the one where the ghoul bargains with different vampires for for stores of blood. He's not going 1 mission a month he'd run out of new vampires super fast and end up bound.<br /> <br /> If someone can point to anywhere in the text where it states the vampire has to feed him directly each and every month with the specific intent of the BP being to make him a ghoul I would guess it is part of 5th edition which is an almost entirely different game. Also forget long distance travel plans what if something just came up for a few days? Ghoul dust when he gets back from some minor delay? or do you have to feed your ghoul every 2-3 weeks to be safe. That would be quite a bit more taxing if you had many ghouls. Regardless The rules don't bare out the opinion it has to be a special in the moment direct feeding to keep a ghoul a ghoul. It's made up till someone drops proof. If I'm wrong put up the edition and page number that states it, I'll look it up provided it's not 5th.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T10:30:18-07:00","id":1511882,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting that blood bonds last significantly longer and you only need a drop, not a full point. It's rare that most characters will want more ghouls than they can count on one hand, so it's not too much of a burden to adequately feed the ones you do full-ghoul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T11:25:36-07:00","id":1511893,"title":"","content":"Sure, I agree with that. If however you have a very old ghoul you'll want to keep him stocked up so a couple centuries don't turn to dust because you were a couple days late. I think there's a reason the Blood Pool of a ghoul goes up 1 each century.<br /> <br /> A point I forgot to make was you don't even need to do anything special to make a vampire let alone a ghoul, any Vitae will do. Shovel Heads from the Sabbat, the origins of the Baali, but I do think it's reasonable to change that or the thing with ghouls if you want. I read one person who said he made it so you had to spend a permanent Willpower point to make another vampire and spend a temporary Willpower to keep a ghoul going each month. As far as the rules go though, things like that aren't required.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}